docs {
  A single-member household with enough answered to fully resolve.
  Every field name comes from the engine-input catalog
  (docs/engine-inputs.json); disqualifier flags are explicitly false
  (no-guess: they are never defaulted), and the empty jobs/assets/
  caregiverRelationships arrays are explicit "none" answers — omitting
  them would leave those collections unacknowledged and the
  determination pending.

  asOf pins the evaluation date to the application filing date so the
  amounts below are reproducible; drop it and proration follows
  today's date instead.

  Expected: determinations[0].status "approved", benefitAmount 200,
  proratedFirstMonthAmount 106 (prorated from the June 15 filing
  date), isExpedited false. No missingInputs.
  Every disqualifier/composition question is answered explicitly:
  under the finality gate a decided status is only returned when no
  unanswered question could change it, so an approved demo must leave
  nothing unanswered.
}
